602	/**
603	 * A single remote command can legitimately run for MINUTES — `apt-get install`,
604	 * `docker save | ssh | docker load`, `certbot certonly`. During that time the
605	 * engine emits nothing, so the customer's progress bar freezes and the run looks
606	 * hung.
607	 *
608	 * Seen live on 2026-07-25: the run sat silent on 89% "Securing your site…" for a
609	 * full TEN MINUTES while a certbot install blocked on needrestart. The customer
610	 * had no way to tell a wedged migration from a slow one.
611	 *
612	 * So the long steps run inside this wrapper, which emits ONE cheap line every
613	 * `everyMs` naming what is still running and for how long. It is deliberately
614	 * dumb: no extra SSH traffic, no state on the target, and a failing `say` can
615	 * never affect the work it is narrating.
616	 */
617	const HEARTBEAT_MS = 45_000;
